description:
Build the future of electromobility with us – in Debrecen!

The world’s leading battery manufacturer, CATL, is opening its second European production base in Debrecen! Be part of an innovative, green, and forward-looking industrial revolution, and join us in shaping Europe’s sustainable mobility!

What tasks await you?

• Consistency correction of warehousing items and document information, including verification of goods, quantities, batches, logos, documents, inspection of packaging appearance, handling of abnormal problems, and completion the system receipt and posting;

• Safely moving the items (raw materials, packaging materials, etc.) from local commodities to designated areas or locations, including the delivery of raw materials, raw material distribution tables, packaging materials, and other inventory materials;

• Operations related to the handling of items such as handling operations in different locations;

• Based on order requirements, inventory picking, inventory disassembly and assembly, system loading and unloading, items and goods, appearance identification;

• Docking and execution of internal pre-inspection of export goods and customs commodity inspection, follow-up processing of abnormal problems, and ensuring that export goods comply with commodity inspection requirements;

• Responsible for the feedback of information required for OL commodity inspection declaration (such as PN/number of cartons/carton PI/gross and net weight, etc...).

You are the perfect candidate if you have:

• Forklift license: 3324, 3312, 3313;

• Positive attitude, clear and logical thinking;

• Willingness to work multiple shifts (12 hours shifts);

• Commitment to work in Debrecen.

• Speaks fluently in hungarian.

What we offer you:

• Bonus: We reward your work with two annual bonuses;

• Cafeteria (SZÉP Card): A monthly cafeteria benefit that you can freely use for leisure or cultural expenses;

• Meal Support: We cover half the cost of one main meal per day – you can choose from both Hungarian and Chinese menus to keep you energized;

• Commuting Support: Company bus or fuel allowance to ensure a smooth commute every day;

• Employee Referral Program: You recommend, we pay;

• Internal Training: We provide in-house training to support your professional development.

Operator

Build the future of electromobility with us – in Debrecen!
The world’s leading battery manufacturer, CATL, is opening its second European production base in Debrecen! Be part of an innovative, green, and forward-looking industrial revolution, and join us in shaping Europe’s sustainable mobility!

What tasks await you?

• Ensuring continuous production and monitoring the operation of production machines;

• Manufacturing products in line with the quality and quantity requirements defined in work instructions;

• Operating, supplying, and overseeing the machines;

• Detecting and reporting technical issues to the relevant colleagues;

• Maintaining cleanliness and order at the workstations and throughout the production environment, in line with 5S standards;

• Supporting compliance with cleanliness rules and their enforcement when working in cleanroom environments;

• Following occupational safety regulations to ensure safe working conditions;

• Accurately maintaining production documentation;

• Actively participating in the training of new colleagues.

You are the perfect candidate if you:

• Have elementary education;

• Have experience working in a production environment;

• Are familiar with fundamental production standards and the 5S system;

• Can confidently use a computer at user level;

• Work well in a team;

• Are persistent, and can handle monotony and stress effectively;

• Perform your tasks in accordance with work instructions;

• Are open to shift work (12-hour standing shifts);

• Are willing to work in Debrecen.

It’s an advantage if you have the following:

• Manufacturing experience in the automotive, food, or chemical industry;

• Experience in battery manufacturing.

What we offer you:

• Bonus: We reward your work with two annual bonuses;

• Cafeteria (SZÉP Card): A monthly cafeteria benefit that you can freely use for leisure or cultural expenses;

• Meal Support: We cover half the cost of one main meal per day – you can choose from both Hungarian and Chinese menus to keep you energized;

• Commuting Support: Company bus or fuel allowance to ensure a smooth commute every day;

• Employee Referral Program: You recommend, we pay;

• Internal Training: We provide in-house training to support your professional development.

