Your tasks will be:

• Conduct safety inspections and audits, drive completion of corrective actions;

• Write safety reports and communicate them to stakeholders;

• Assist in implementation of safety management system and programs, like safety training, emergency drills, fire safety management;

• Support safety engineer to develop and implement annual emergency drill plan;

• Purchase materials or service that EHS department needs, including but not limited to PPE, firefighting equipment, labels, first aid supplies, etc;

• Assist safety engineer completing regulatory compliance tasks on time;

• Manage inventory of PPE, firefighting equipment, emergency response materials, etc;

• Oversee the safety management of contractors on site;

• Provide training and safety education to employees;

• Other tasks assigned by EHS manager and safety engineer.

You are the perfect candidate if:

• You have a high school or bachelor degree in in the field of safety engineering/technology, fire protection, industrial engineering, mechanical engineering or equivalent experience;

• You have 1-3 years of EHS work experience;

• You posess knowledge of labor protection and occupational health regulation and legislation;

• Basic knowledge of ISO 45001;

• Knowledge of preparing an occupational health and safety risk assessment;

• Basic knowledge of fire protection legal requirements;

• Knowledge of machine and equipment commissioning requirements is an advantage;

• Ability to work in a challenging and fast paced, collaborative environment and creatively problem-solve.

An Advantage:

• Experience in the battery, chemical or automotive industry or equivalent experience;

• Fluency in English.

What we provide:

• Bonus: We reward your work with two annual bonuses;

• Cafeteria (SZÉP Card): A monthly cafeteria benefit that you can freely use for leisure or cultural expenses;

