• Possess programming and troubleshooting capabilities with at least two mainstream PLC platforms (such as Siemens, Mitsubishi, Omron, Schneider, or Keyence), and have strong analytical and problem-solving skills;

• Demonstrate good leadership, teamwork, reporting, and cross-functional communication abilities, with fluent English and Hungarian language skills.

It’s an advantage if you have the following:

• Experience in intelligent manufacturing, Industry 4.0, battery, automotive, electronics, or other high-volume manufacturing industries;

• Knowledge of programming languages (C language, LabVIEW), CCD vision systems, TPM, lean manufacturing, or energy management.

