• Performing live-line working operations, provided you hold the required qualifications, internal competencies, and employer authorizations;

• Participating in pilot production runs, the introduction of new products and manufacturing processes, as well as inspection and repair tasks;

• Maintaining accurate production documentation and recording data in production systems;

• Complying with occupational health and safety, electrical safety, and 5S requirements.

You are the perfect candidate if you:

• Speak Hungarian fluently;

• Hold a completed vocational qualification in power electrical engineering, such as:

• Electrician

• Electrical Machine and Equipment Technician

• Mining Electrical Technician

• Power Electrical Engineering Technician

• Another qualification in power electrical engineering, electrical engineering, or building electrical systems;

• Have at least one year of relevant professional experience in power electrical engineering;

• Maintain accurate documentation and have basic computer skills;

• Are willing to complete the required professional, electrical safety, and live-line working training;

• Are willing to work 12-hour shifts on a rotating multi-shift schedule in Debrecen.

